  "title": "# Activity banner fix (Brett, Oct 31 night) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md and _clau…",
  "asked": "# Activity banner fix (Brett, Oct 31 night) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md and _claude/persona.md first. Opus, one session. Git login works: plain `git push`. Read the read-only diagnosis first: /root/axf-builds/banner-check/_claude/builds/reports/banner-check.md (and banner-check.log). Problem: the console activity banner shows 28 in progress / 21 stuck, but only ~5 lines are real. ~46 ghosts are command lines (git push/pull/merge, rm, builds) from Claude Code hooks that never close, because PostToolUse isn't registered in ~/.claude/settings.json. It also counts `git merge-base` as Merging and `rm /tmp/...` as Deleting, shows each session twice (session + its change-log entry), and the open banner takes ~47% of the screen. Fix: 1. Re-register the hooks (activity.mjs hooks install) so PostToolUse is back for root and axfbuild; make claude-headless.sh sessions get them too. Add a systems-check banner item that goes red when hook events stop arriving or PostToolUse is missing, with Auto fix. 2. On Stop/SessionEnd, close every command line that session left open. Command lines expire after ~5 min without word; hide them once their session ended. Clear the existing ghosts on deploy. 3. Tighten matching: merge-base, rev-parse, log, status, diff are reads, not Merging; rm of /tmp or a build's scratch files is not Deleting. 4. One row per session (fold its change-log entry into it). 5. Banner starts collapsed to one line (counts only); open max ~30% of the screen, scroll inside. Framework controls + theme/scale tokens only. 6. The GitHub part of the banner gets 403 on all 3 repos: find which token it uses and why (scope, fine-grained repo access, or rate limit); point it at the working GITHUB_TOKEN in /opt/axf/.axf-console/secrets.env (never print it) or put a precise banner item saying what permission is missing. 7. Point the holds check at the builds store, not the old pending.json export. Tests for each (ghost closing, expiry, matching, one row per session, collapsed height). Full local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle checks (machine-only failures that also fail on clean main are fine; say so). Phone + desktop screenshots, before/after, to UI Review via framework/cli/shot.mjs, group 'Banner fix - Oct 31 night'. Commit, fetch+merge origin/main, retest, `git push origin HEAD:main` (never force). Plain-English report at _claude/builds/reports/banner-fix.md: each item, what was wrong, what changed, before/after numbers. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault).",
